Description:

Request bodies received over HTTP/2 are now bounded by
:imapdconf:`maxmessagesize`, as bodies received over HTTP/1.x already were.
A request whose body exceeds the limit is answered with 413 (Content Too
Large).  Previously the DATA frame handler appended every payload to the body
with no size check at all.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-8hmh-f4jx-29pm.


